-- The internal extension of the parsed AST: the expressions the elaboration adds.
-- expr and setexpr extend the exact bases in syntax.terms; their old
-- constructors embed by identity and are not repeated or regenerated here.
-- External primitives: reference = existing Identity or nonempty string;
-- resolved_input = the existing native.records.ResolvedName.
-- Expression positions additionally admit retained setexpr, resolved_input,
-- and native.predicates.Predicate values (the existing internal record forms).
-- binding is a tuple product, not an additional constructor class.
-- Unresolved inhabits both existing bases; it is emitted once under expr.
-- This is an internal extension profile, with no concrete source spellings.
-- StochasticKernelSet(H, Z) denotes probability kernels from H to Z: for each measurable
-- B in Z, h maps to P(h, B) measurably. It does not impose a chosen sigma
-- algebra on the set ProbabilityMeasureSet(Z). typing.primitive_definitions._kernel
-- expands this meaning into FunctionSet, ProbabilityMeasureSet and MeasurableMapSet expressions.
--
-- Constructor checking requires immutable children and typed bindings with
-- distinct identities within one Lambda. Domains are set expressions.
-- Every binding scopes over body only. All Lambda domains are outside its
-- scope; Integral.measure is outside its scope too. Measure's binding domain
-- specifies measurable subsets of domain (countable additivity is a rule
-- requirement, not established by constructing this expression).
-- Nested scopes can shadow identities. Alpha comparison and substitution
-- enforce these scopes separately from the first-order ASDL field structure.
-- Unresolved.missing is a nonempty description such as arguments or results.
-- Compose(outer, inner, outputs) is the composition outer ∘ inner of two maps
-- held by reference: outputs are the coordinates the
-- inner map writes, one binding each, which bind nothing inside the term; a
-- consumer that applies the composition at a point reads outer(inner(p)), and,
-- where the inner map writes several coordinates, the let-form
-- ((outputs) ↦ outer(outputs))(inner(p)), so that the record names the
-- coordinates and no projection is written.
-- ProductMeasure(binding, body) is the finite product of the probability
-- measures body(i), i in the binding's domain I, a finite set: the unique
-- probability measure on the functions e : I -> Z, with the sigma algebra the
-- coordinate maps generate, whose value at every rectangle
-- {e | e(i) in B_i for all i in I} is the product over i of body(i)(B_i). The
-- binding's domain is outside its scope; the body may read the index, parents
-- and parameters, never another coordinate. For empty I it is the point mass
-- on the empty function.

module semantic
{
  binding = (resolved_input variable, setexpr domain)

  expr = Apply(expr function, expr* args)
       | Lambda(binding* bindings, expr body)
       | Compose(expr outer, expr inner, binding* outputs)
       | Integral(binding binding, expr measure, expr body)
       | Sup(binding binding, expr body)
       | Measure(setexpr domain, binding binding, expr body)
       | ProductMeasure(binding binding, expr body)
       | Unresolved(reference identity, string missing)

  setexpr = FunctionSet(setexpr domain, setexpr codomain)
          | MeasurableMapSet(setexpr domain, setexpr codomain)
          | StochasticKernelSet(setexpr domain, setexpr codomain)
          | FiniteMeasureSet(setexpr domain)
          | ProbabilityMeasureSet(setexpr domain)
          | PowerSet(setexpr domain)
}
